\f0\fs24 \cf0 Trapping Rain Water \
\
Rain water gets trapped when there is a level between two other levels such that the middle level is lower than both levels. \
\
If there are levels within levels, we are interested in increasing the area, so the farther apart and the higher the outer levels, the more we favor them \
\
The outermost positions can trap water only on the inside of them and not use the void as a post. \
\
